Fixed and verified.

The bug was in `advanceTurn` at `src/sim.ts:43`. Population growth was gated on `foodSurplus >= 0`, which counts a break-even turn (production exactly equals consumption) as growth. The docstring says population grows on a food **surplus**, which means production must strictly exceed consumption.

Change: `if (foodSurplus >= 0)` → `if (foodSurplus > 0)`.

Verification:
- `npm run typecheck` — passes
- `npm test` — 4/4 tests pass

A settlement now only grows when it has a genuine food surplus; break-even and deficit settlements hold steady.


